      ],
      note:'The constraint that you cannot paint white over colour fundamentally changes the conceptual order of working. Oil painters work dark to light; watercolourists must plan every light area before they begin. This is why experienced watercolourists work in a completely different order from oil painters — and why crossing between the two media is genuinely difficult to learn.'
