      look:'Do not look at the smile. Look at the horizon line: the landscape on the left sits noticeably higher than on the right. This asymmetry destabilises the composition and creates the uncanny spatial unease the painting is famous for. Then look at what is not there: no visible brushstrokes anywhere in the face. None.'
